{"id":"mahabharata-1-057","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":57,"title":"सप्तपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 57 · Uparichara Vasu and the births of Satyavati and Vyasa","summary":{"en":"King Uparichara Vasu receives a crystal chariot from Indra; his seed, carried by a hawk, falls into the Yamuna, where the fish-nymph Adrika bears twins, Matsya and Satyavati. Satyavati, raised by a fisherman, bears Vyasa to the sage Parashara, and the births of the epic's heroes are briefly listed.","kn":"ಉಪರಿಚರ ವಸುರಾಜನು ಇಂದ್ರನಿಂದ ಸ್ಫಟಿಕ ವಿಮಾನ ಪಡೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಗಿಡುಗ ಒಯ್ದ ಅವನ ವೀರ್ಯ ಯಮುನೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಬಿದ್ದು ಮೀನಿನ ರೂಪದ ಅಪ್ಸರೆ ಅದ್ರಿಕೆ ಮತ್ಸ್ಯ ಸತ್ಯವತಿ ಎಂಬ ಅವಳಿಗಳನ್ನು ಹೆರುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಬೆಸ್ತನಿಂದ ಬೆಳೆದ ಸತ್ಯವತಿ ಪರಾಶರ ಋಷಿಯಿಂದ ವ್ಯಾಸರನ್ನು ಹೆರುತ್ತಾಳೆ; ಮಹಾಕಾವ್ಯದ ವೀರರ ಜನನಗಳನ್ನು ಸಂಕ್ಷೇಪವಾಗಿ ಹೇಳಲಾಗಿದೆ.","hi":"राजा उपरिचर वसु को इन्द्र से स्फटिक का विमान मिलता है; बाज़ द्वारा ले जाया गया उनका वीर्य यमुना में गिरता है, जहाँ मछली बनी अप्सरा अद्रिका मत्स्य और सत्यवती नामक जुड़वाँ को जन्म देती है। मछुए द्वारा पाली गई सत्यवती ऋषि पराशर से व्यास को जन्म देती है, और महाकाव्य के वीरों के जन्म संक्षेप में गिनाए जाते हैं।","te":"ఉపరిచర వసురాజు ఇంద్రుని నుండి స్ఫటిక విమానం పొందుతాడు; డేగ మోసుకుపోయిన అతని వీర్యం యమునలో పడగా చేపరూపంలోని అప్సరస అద్రిక మత్స్యుడు, సత్యవతి అనే కవలలను కంటుంది. జాలరి పెంచిన సత్యవతి పరాశర మహర్షి వల్ల వ్యాసుని కంటుంది; మహాకావ్య వీరుల జననాలు సంక్షిప్తంగా చెప్పబడతాయి.","ta":"உபரிசர வஸு மன்னன் இந்திரனிடமிருந்து பளிங்கு விமானம் பெறுகிறான்; பருந்து கொண்டு சென்ற அவன் விந்து யமுனையில் விழ, மீன் வடிவிலிருந்த அப்ஸரஸ் அத்ரிகை மத்ஸ்யன், ஸத்யவதி என்ற இரட்டையரைப் பெறுகிறாள். மீனவனால் வளர்க்கப்பட்ட ஸத்யவதி பராஶர முனிவரால் வியாஸரைப் பெறுகிறாள்; காவிய வீரர்களின் பிறப்புகள் சுருக்கமாகக் குறிப்பிடப்படுகின்றன.","ml":"ഉപരിചരവസു രാജാവിന് ഇന്ദ്രനിൽ നിന്ന് സ്ഫടികരഥം ലഭിക്കുന്നു; പരുന്ത് വഹിച്ചുകൊണ്ടുപോയ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ ബീജം യമുനയിൽ വീഴുന്നു, അവിടെ അദ്രിക എന്ന മത്സ്യകന്യക ഇരട്ടകളെ പ്രസവിക്കുന്നു: മത്സ്യനും സത്യവതിയും. മത്സ്യബന്ധനക്കാരൻ വളർത്തിയ സത്യവതി പരാശരനിൽ നിന്ന് വ്യാസനെ പ്രസവിക്കുന്നു; ഇതിഹാസത്തിലെ നായകന്മാരുടെ ജനനവും ചുരുക്കി പറയപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.57; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"अंशावतरणपर्व","titleEn":"Amshavatarana Parva (Partial incarnations)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"राजोपरिचरो नाम धर्मनित्यो महीपतिः ।\nबभूव मृगयां गन्तुं स कदाचिद्धृतव्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was a king named Uparichara, ever devoted to dharma, firm in his vows; once he went out hunting."}},{"n":2,"text":"स चेदिविषयं रम्यं वसुः पौरवनन्दनः ।\nइन्द्रोपदेशाज्जग्राह ग्रहणीयं महीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That Vasu, delight of the Pauravas, at Indra's counsel took possession of the lovely land of Chedi, a land worth taking."}},{"n":3,"text":"तमाश्रमे न्यस्तशस्त्रं निवसन्तं तपोरतिम् ।\nदेवः साक्षात्स्वयं वज्री समुपायान्महीपतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While he lived in a hermitage, having laid down his weapons and delighting in austerity, the god himself, the thunderbolt-wielder, approached that king."}},{"n":4,"text":"इन्द्रत्वमर्हो राजायं तपसेत्यनुचिन्त्य वै ।\nतं सान्त्वेन नृपं साक्षात्तपसः संन्यवर्तयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking that this king deserved Indra's own rank through austerity, Indra gently turned him back from his penance."}},{"text":"इन्द्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Indra said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"न संकीर्येत धर्मोऽयं पृथिव्यां पृथिवीपते ।\nतं पाहि धर्मो हि धृतः कृत्स्नं धारयते जगत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the earth, let dharma on earth not be thrown into confusion; protect it, for dharma upheld upholds the whole world."}},{"n":6,"text":"लोक्यं धर्मं पालय त्वं नित्ययुक्तः समाहितः ।\nधर्मयुक्तस्ततो लोकान्पुण्यानाप्स्यसि शाश्वतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Protect the dharma that benefits the world, always attentive and composed; joined to dharma, you will gain holy, everlasting worlds."}},{"n":7,"text":"दिविष्ठस्य भुविष्ठस्त्वं सखा भूत्वा मम प्रियः ।\nऊधः पृथिव्या यो देशस्तमावस नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"You on earth, I in heaven: be my dear friend. Live in the country that is the udder of the earth, lord of men."}},{"n":8,"text":"पशव्यश्चैव पुण्यश्च सुस्थिरो धनधान्यवान् ।\nस्वारक्ष्यश्चैव सौम्यश्च भोग्यैर्भूमिगुणैर्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is good for cattle, holy, very stable, rich in wealth and grain, easy to guard and gentle, endowed with the earth's enjoyable qualities."}},{"n":9,"text":"अत्यन्यानेष देशो हि धनरत्नादिभिर्युतः ।\nवसुपूर्णा च वसुधा वस चेदिषु चेदिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"That land surpasses others in wealth, jewels and the rest; the earth is full of treasure. Live among the Chedis, king of Chedi."}},{"n":10,"text":"धर्मशीला जनपदाः सुसंतोषाश्च साधवः ।\nन च मिथ्याप्रलापोऽत्र स्वैरेष्वपि कुतोऽन्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The countries there are devoted to dharma, the good people well content; no false speech is heard there, not even in jest, much less otherwise."}},{"n":11,"text":"न च पित्रा विभज्यन्ते नरा गुरुहिते रताः ।\nयुञ्जते धुरि नो गाश्च कृशाः संधुक्षयन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men devoted to their elders' welfare are not divided from their fathers; they do not yoke even lean cows to the yoke, and they feed them well."}},{"n":12,"text":"सर्वे वर्णाः स्वधर्मस्थाः सदा चेदिषु मानद ।\nन तेऽस्त्यविदितं किंचित्त्रिषु लोकेषु यद्भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the Chedi land, giver of honor, all the classes always stay in their own duties. There is nothing in the three worlds that is unknown to you."}},{"n":13,"text":"देवोपभोग्यं दिव्यं च आकाशे स्फाटिकं महत् ।\nआकाशगं त्वां मद्दत्तं विमानमुपपत्स्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great divine crystal aerial car, fit for the gods' enjoyment and moving through the sky, given by me, will come to you."}},{"n":14,"text":"त्वमेकः सर्वमर्त्येषु विमानवरमास्थितः ।\nचरिष्यस्युपरिस्थो वै देवो विग्रहवानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"You alone among mortals, seated in the finest of chariots, will travel above, like a god in bodily form."}},{"n":15,"text":"ददामि ते वैजयन्तीं मालामम्लानपङ्कजाम् ।\nधारयिष्यति संग्रामे या त्वां शस्त्रैरविक्षतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I give you the Vaijayanti garland of unfading lotuses, which will keep you unwounded by weapons in battle."}},{"n":16,"text":"लक्षणं चैतदेवेह भविता ते नराधिप ।\nइन्द्रमालेति विख्यातं धन्यमप्रतिमं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And this will be your mark here, lord of men: the great, blessed, matchless garland known as Indra's garland."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"यष्टिं च वैणवीं तस्मै ददौ वृत्रनिषूदनः ।\nइष्टप्रदानमुद्दिश्य शिष्टानां परिपालिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The slayer of Vritra also gave him a bamboo staff, to protect the good, for the sake of the favors he gave."}},{"n":18,"text":"तस्याः शक्रस्य पूजार्थं भूमौ भूमिपतिस्तदा ।\nप्रवेशं कारयामास गते संवत्सरे तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"To honor Indra, the king had that staff planted in the ground when a year had gone by."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततः प्रभृति चाद्यापि यष्ट्याः क्षितिपसत्तमैः ।\nप्रवेशः क्रियते राजन्यथा तेन प्रवर्तितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From then until today, best of kings, the best of kings plant the staff, as he established it."}},{"n":20,"text":"अपरेद्युस्तथा चास्याः क्रियते उच्छ्रयो नृपैः ।\nअलंकृतायाः पिटकैर्गन्धैर्माल्यैश्च भूषणैः ।\nमाल्यदामपरिक्षिप्ता विधिवत्क्रियतेऽपि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the next day, kings raise it up, adorned with cloths, perfumes, garlands and ornaments, and wrapped in strings of flowers, as the rule requires."}},{"n":21,"text":"भगवान्पूज्यते चात्र हास्यरूपेण शंकरः ।\nस्वयमेव गृहीतेन वसोः प्रीत्या महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There also the lord Shankara is worshipped in a comic form, himself taking part, out of love for the great-souled Vasu."}},{"n":22,"text":"एतां पूजां महेन्द्रस्तु दृष्ट्वा देव कृतां शुभाम् ।\nवसुना राजमुख्येन प्रीतिमानब्रवीद्विभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing this auspicious worship, performed by Vasu, the best of kings, mighty Indra was pleased and said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"ये पूजयिष्यन्ति नरा राजानश्च महं मम ।\nकारयिष्यन्ति च मुदा यथा चेदिपतिर्नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Those men and kings who worship my festival and gladly have it held, as the king of Chedi did,"}},{"n":24,"text":"तेषां श्रीर्विजयश्चैव सराष्ट्राणां भविष्यति ।\nतथा स्फीतो जनपदो मुदितश्च भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"will have fortune and victory, and their realms too; their country will prosper and be happy.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"एवं महात्मना तेन महेन्द्रेण नराधिप ।\nवसुः प्रीत्या मघवता महाराजोऽभिसत्कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus, lord of men, the great Indra with love honored the great king Vasu."}},{"n":26,"text":"उत्सवं कारयिष्यन्ति सदा शक्रस्य ये नराः ।\nभूमिदानादिभिर्दानैर्यथा पूता भवन्ति वै ।\nवरदानमहायज्ञैस्तथा शक्रोत्सवेन ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who always hold the festival of Indra are purified by it, as by gifts such as gifts of land and the great sacrifices of boon-giving."}},{"n":27,"text":"संपूजितो मघवता वसुश्चेदिपतिस्तदा ।\nपालयामास धर्मेण चेदिस्थः पृथिवीमिमाम् ।\nइन्द्रप्रीत्या भूमिपतिश्चकारेन्द्रमहं वसुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honored by Indra, Vasu, king of Chedi, dwelling in Chedi, ruled this earth in dharma. In gratitude to Indra, the king Vasu held the festival of Indra."}},{"n":28,"text":"पुत्राश्चास्य महावीर्याः पञ्चासन्नमितौजसः ।\nनानाराज्येषु च सुतान्स सम्राडभ्यषेचयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He had five sons of great strength and boundless power, and that emperor anointed his sons in various kingdoms."}},{"n":29,"text":"महारथो मगधराड्विश्रुतो यो बृहद्रथः ।\nप्रत्यग्रहः कुशाम्बश्च यमाहुर्मणिवाहनम् ।\nमच्छिल्लश्च यदुश्चैव राजन्यश्चापराजितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were Brihadratha, the famous great chariot-warrior and king of Magadha; Pratyagraha; Kushamba, whom they call Manivahana; Machchhilla; and Yadu, and the unconquered Rajanya."}},{"n":30,"text":"एते तस्य सुता राजन्राजर्षेर्भूरितेजसः ।\nन्यवेशयन्नामभिः स्वैस्ते देशांश्च पुराणि च ।\nवासवाः पञ्च राजानः पृथग्वंशाश्च शाश्वताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These, king, were the sons of that royal sage of great splendor. They founded lands and cities under their own names: five Vasava kings, with separate lines that endured."}},{"n":31,"text":"वसन्तमिन्द्रप्रासादे आकाशे स्फाटिके च तम् ।\nउपतस्थुर्महात्मानं गन्धर्वाप्सरसो नृपम् ।\nराजोपरिचरेत्येवं नाम तस्याथ विश्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he lived in Indra's palace, in the crystal car in the sky, the Gandharvas and apsarases waited on that great-souled king, and so his name became famed as Uparichara, \"he who moves above.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"पुरोपवाहिनीं तस्य नदीं शुक्तिमतीं गिरिः ।\nअरौत्सीच्चेतनायुक्तः कामात्कोलाहलः किल ॥","meaning":{"en":"A mountain named Kolahala, moved by desire and endowed with feeling, once blocked the river Shuktimati, which flowed beside his city."}},{"n":33,"text":"गिरिं कोलाहलं तं तु पदा वसुरताडयत् ।\nनिश्चक्राम नदी तेन प्रहारविवरेण सा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasu struck the mountain Kolahala with his foot, and the river came out through the gap made by the blow."}},{"n":34,"text":"तस्यां नद्यामजनयन्मिथुनं पर्वतः स्वयम् ।\nतस्माद्विमोक्षणात्प्रीता नदी राज्ञे न्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mountain himself had begotten a pair of twins in that river; pleased at her release, the river told the king."}},{"n":35,"text":"यः पुमानभवत्तत्र तं स राजर्षिसत्तमः ।\nवसुर्वसुप्रदश्चक्रे सेनापतिमरिंदमम् ।\nचकार पत्नीं कन्यां तु दयितां गिरिकां नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The male child, the best of royal sages Vasu, the giver of wealth, made commander of his army, a subduer of foes. The female he took as his beloved wife, Girika."}},{"n":36,"text":"वसोः पत्नी तु गिरिका कामात्काले न्यवेदयत् ।\nऋतुकालमनुप्राप्तं स्नाता पुंसवने शुचिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasu's wife Girika, from desire, told him at the right time that she had reached her fertile season, bathed and pure, ready for conceiving a son."}},{"n":37,"text":"तदहः पितरश्चैनमूचुर्जहि मृगानिति ।\nतं राजसत्तमं प्रीतास्तदा मतिमतां वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That same day the ancestors said to him, \"Kill deer,\" pleased with that best of kings, supreme among the wise."}},{"n":38,"text":"स पितॄणां नियोगं तमव्यतिक्रम्य पार्थिवः ।\nचचार मृगयां कामी गिरिकामेव संस्मरन् ।\nअतीव रूपसंपन्नां साक्षाच्छ्रियमिवापराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king did not disobey the order of the ancestors. He went hunting with desire, remembering only Girika, who was very beautiful, like a second Shri herself."}},{"n":39,"text":"तस्य रेतः प्रचस्कन्द चरतो रुचिरे वने ।\nस्कन्नमात्रं च तद्रेतो वृक्षपत्रेण भूमिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he roamed in the lovely forest, his seed fell. As soon as it fell, the king caught the seed on a tree leaf,"}},{"n":40,"text":"प्रतिजग्राह मिथ्या मे न स्कन्देद्रेत इत्युत ।\nऋतुश्च तस्याः पत्न्या मे न मोघः स्यादिति प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"thinking, \"Let my seed not fall in vain, and let my wife's fertile season not be wasted.\""}},{"n":41,"text":"संचिन्त्यैवं तदा राजा विचार्य च पुनः पुनः ।\nअमोघत्वं च विज्ञाय रेतसो राजसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking thus, again and again, and knowing that his seed was unfailing, that best of kings,"}},{"n":42,"text":"शुक्रप्रस्थापने कालं महिष्याः प्रसमीक्ष्य सः ।\nअभिमन्त्र्याथ तच्छुक्रमारात्तिष्ठन्तमाशुगम् ।\nसूक्ष्मधर्मार्थतत्त्वज्ञो ज्ञात्वा श्येनं ततोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"seeing that it was the time for sending seed to his queen, consecrated the seed with a mantra, knowing the subtle truth of dharma and profit. Seeing a swift hawk standing nearby, he said to it:"}},{"n":43,"text":"मत्प्रियार्थमिदं सौम्य शुक्रं मम गृहं नय ।\nगिरिकायाः प्रयच्छाशु तस्या ह्यार्तवमद्य वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Gentle one, for my sake take this seed to my house and quickly give it to Girika, for today is her fertile time.\""}},{"n":44,"text":"गृहीत्वा तत्तदा श्येनस्तूर्णमुत्पत्य वेगवान् ।\nजवं परममास्थाय प्रदुद्राव विहंगमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The swift hawk took it, flew up quickly, and sped away at the highest speed."}},{"n":45,"text":"तमपश्यदथायान्तं श्येनं श्येनस्तथापरः ।\nअभ्यद्रवच्च तं सद्यो दृष्ट्वैवामिषशङ्कया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Another hawk saw him coming and, suspecting he carried meat, at once flew at him."}},{"n":46,"text":"तुण्डयुद्धमथाकाशे तावुभौ संप्रचक्रतुः ।\nयुध्यतोरपतद्रेतस्तच्चापि यमुनाम्भसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two fought with beaks in the sky, and as they fought the seed fell into the waters of the Yamuna."}},{"n":47,"text":"तत्राद्रिकेति विख्याता ब्रह्मशापाद्वराप्सराः ।\nमीनभावमनुप्राप्ता बभूव यमुनाचरी ॥","meaning":{"en":"There an excellent apsaras named Adrika, famed, who by a Brahmin's curse had become a fish, lived in the Yamuna."}},{"n":48,"text":"श्येनपादपरिभ्रष्टं तद्वीर्यमथ वासवम् ।\nजग्राह तरसोपेत्य साद्रिका मत्स्यरूपिणी ॥","meaning":{"en":"The seed of Vasava, slipped from the hawk's claws, was swiftly seized by Adrika in her fish form."}},{"n":49,"text":"कदाचिदथ मत्सीं तां बबन्धुर्मत्स्यजीविनः ।\nमासे च दशमे प्राप्ते तदा भरतसत्तम ।\nउज्जह्रुरुदरात्तस्याः स्त्रीपुमांसं च मानुषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some time later fishermen caught that fish. When the tenth month came, best of the Bharatas, they took from her belly a boy and a girl, human."}},{"n":50,"text":"आश्चर्यभूतं मत्वा तद्राज्ञस्ते प्रत्यवेदयन् ।\nकाये मत्स्या इमौ राजन्संभूतौ मानुषाविति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking it a marvel, they reported to the king: \"King, these two humans were born in the body of a fish.\""}},{"n":51,"text":"तयोः पुमांसं जग्राह राजोपरिचरस्तदा ।\nस मत्स्यो नाम राजासीद्धार्मिकः सत्यसंगरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king Uparichara took the boy of the two. He became King Matsya, righteous and true to his word."}},{"n":52,"text":"साप्सरा मुक्तशापा च क्षणेन समपद्यत ।\nपुरोक्ता या भगवता तिर्यग्योनिगता शुभे ।\nमानुषौ जनयित्वा त्वं शापमोक्षमवाप्स्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the apsaras was freed of the curse in an instant. As the holy one had told her before, \"Having gone into an animal womb, once you give birth to two humans, you will be freed from the curse.\""}},{"n":53,"text":"ततः सा जनयित्वा तौ विशस्ता मत्स्यघातिना ।\nसंत्यज्य मत्स्यरूपं सा दिव्यं रूपमवाप्य च ।\nसिद्धर्षिचारणपथं जगामाथ वराप्सराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having given birth to them and been cut open by the fisherman, she gave up the fish form, took on a divine form, and the excellent apsaras went by the path of siddhas, sages and charanas."}},{"n":54,"text":"या कन्या दुहिता तस्या मत्स्या मत्स्यसगन्धिनी ।\nराज्ञा दत्ताथ दाशाय इयं तव भवत्विति ।\nरूपसत्त्वसमायुक्ता सर्वैः समुदिता गुणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The girl, her daughter, smelled of fish. The king gave her to the chief of the fishermen, saying, \"She shall be yours,\" a girl endowed with beauty and goodness and with all merits."}},{"n":55,"text":"सा तु सत्यवती नाम मत्स्यघात्यभिसंश्रयात् ।\nआसीन्मत्स्यसगन्धैव कंचित्कालं शुचिस्मिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"She was named Satyavati; living under the fisherman's care, she kept the fish smell for some time, the one of pure smile."}},{"n":56,"text":"शुश्रूषार्थं पितुर्नावं तां तु वाहयतीं जले ।\nतीर्थयात्रां परिक्रामन्नपश्यद्वै पराशरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"To serve her father she used to row a boat on the water; Parashara, going about on pilgrimage, saw her."}},{"n":57,"text":"अतीव रूपसंपन्नां सिद्धानामपि काङ्क्षिताम् ।\nदृष्ट्वैव च स तां धीमांश्चकमे चारुदर्शनाम् ।\nविद्वांस्तां वासवीं कन्यां कार्यवान्मुनिपुंगवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She was very beautiful, desired even by siddhas. At the very sight of her, the wise sage, best of the sages, with his purpose in mind, desired that charming girl, daughter of Vasu."}},{"n":58,"text":"साब्रवीत्पश्य भगवन्पारावारे ऋषीन्स्थितान् ।\nआवयोर्दृश्यतोरेभिः कथं नु स्यात्समागमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She said: \"Look, lord, the sages are standing on the far shore and this one. While they can see us, how could our union happen?\""}},{"n":59,"text":"एवं तयोक्तो भगवान्नीहारमसृजत्प्रभुः ।\nयेन देशः स सर्वस्तु तमोभूत इवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told this, the lord created a mist, and the whole region became as if dark."}},{"n":60,"text":"दृष्ट्वा सृष्टं तु नीहारं ततस्तं परमर्षिणा ।\nविस्मिता चाब्रवीत्कन्या व्रीडिता च मनस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the mist made by the great sage, the girl, astonished and ashamed, though strong-minded, said:"}},{"n":61,"text":"विद्धि मां भगवन्कन्यां सदा पितृवशानुगाम् ।\nत्वत्संयोगाच्च दुष्येत कन्याभावो ममानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Know, lord, that I am a maiden, always under my father's authority. My maidenhood would be spoiled by union with you, blameless one."}},{"n":62,"text":"कन्यात्वे दूषिते चापि कथं शक्ष्ये द्विजोत्तम ।\nगन्तुं गृहं गृहे चाहं धीमन्न स्थातुमुत्सहे ।\nएतत्संचिन्त्य भगवन्विधत्स्व यदनन्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And with my maidenhood spoiled, best of brahmins, how could I go home? I could not bear to stay in my house, wise one. Consider this, lord, and decide what is to follow.\""}},{"n":63,"text":"एवमुक्तवतीं तां तु प्रीतिमानृषिसत्तमः ।\nउवाच मत्प्रियं कृत्वा कन्यैव त्वं भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pleased, the best of sages said to her when she had spoken: \"Having pleased me, you will remain a maiden."}},{"n":64,"text":"वृणीष्व च वरं भीरु यं त्वमिच्छसि भामिनि ।\nवृथा हि न प्रसादो मे भूतपूर्वः शुचिस्मिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"And choose a boon, timid one, whatever you wish, radiant lady. My favor, pure-smiling one, has never been in vain.\""}},{"n":65,"text":"एवमुक्ता वरं वव्रे गात्रसौगन्ध्यमुत्तमम् ।\nस चास्यै भगवान्प्रादान्मनसः काङ्क्षितं प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So told, she chose the best fragrance of her body, and the lord gave her what her heart desired."}},{"n":66,"text":"ततो लब्धवरा प्रीता स्त्रीभावगुणभूषिता ।\nजगाम सह संसर्गमृषिणाद्भुतकर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having gained the boon, pleased and adorned with the qualities of womanhood, she united with the sage of wondrous deeds."}},{"n":67,"text":"तेन गन्धवतीत्येव नामास्याः प्रथितं भुवि ।\nतस्यास्तु योजनाद्गन्धमाजिघ्रन्ति नरा भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"From this her name became known on earth as Gandhavati, the fragrant one; people on earth smell her scent from a yojana away."}},{"n":68,"text":"ततो योजनगन्धेति तस्या नाम परिश्रुतम् ।\nपराशरोऽपि भगवाञ्जगाम स्वं निवेशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then she was famed as Yojanagandha, \"she who is fragrant for a yojana.\" And the lord Parashara went to his own dwelling."}},{"n":69,"text":"इति सत्यवती हृष्टा लब्ध्वा वरमनुत्तमम् ।\nपराशरेण संयुक्ता सद्यो गर्भं सुषाव सा ।\nजज्ञे च यमुनाद्वीपे पाराशर्यः स वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So Satyavati, glad at gaining the unsurpassed boon and united with Parashara, at once bore a child. The mighty son of Parashara was born on an island in the Yamuna."}},{"n":70,"text":"स मातरमुपस्थाय तपस्येव मनो दधे ।\nस्मृतोऽहं दर्शयिष्यामि कृत्येष्विति च सोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He approached his mother and set his mind on austerity, saying: \"When you remember me in need, I will appear.\""}},{"n":71,"text":"एवं द्वैपायनो जज्ञे सत्यवत्यां पराशरात् ।\nद्वीपे न्यस्तः स यद्बालस्तस्माद्द्वैपायनोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus Dvaipayana was born to Satyavati by Parashara. Because that child was placed on an island, he became Dvaipayana, \"island-born.\""}},{"n":72,"text":"पादापसारिणं धर्मं विद्वान्स तु युगे युगे ।\nआयुः शक्तिं च मर्त्यानां युगानुगमवेक्ष्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"In every age, he, the knowing one, seeing dharma losing a quarter and observing the lifespan and strength of mortals as they follow the age,"}},{"n":73,"text":"ब्रह्मणो ब्राह्मणानां च तथानुग्रहकाम्यया ।\nविव्यास वेदान्यस्माच्च तस्माद्व्यास इति स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and wishing to favor Brahma and the brahmins, divided the Vedas; for that reason he is remembered as Vyasa, \"the divider.\""}},{"n":74,"text":"वेदानध्यापयामास महाभारतपञ्चमान् ।\nसुमन्तुं जैमिनिं पैलं शुकं चैव स्वमात्मजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He taught the Vedas, with the Mahabharata as the fifth, to Sumantu, Jaimini, Paila, and his own son Shuka,"}},{"n":75,"text":"प्रभुर्वरिष्ठो वरदो वैशंपायनमेव च ।\nसंहितास्तैः पृथक्त्वेन भारतस्य प्रकाशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and to Vaishampayana as well; the mighty one, the best, the giver of boons. By them the versions of the Bharata were made known separately."}},{"n":76,"text":"तथा भीष्मः शांतनवो गङ्गायाममितद्युतिः ।\nवसुवीर्यात्समभवन्महावीर्यो महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise Bhishma, son of Shantanu, of boundless brilliance, great strength and great fame, was born of Ganga from a portion of the Vasu."}},{"n":77,"text":"शूले प्रोतः पुराणर्षिरचोरश्चोरशङ्कया ।\nअणीमाण्डव्य इति वै विख्यातः सुमहायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"An ancient sage, though no thief, was impaled on a stake on suspicion of theft; he became famed as Animandavya, of very great renown."}},{"n":78,"text":"स धर्ममाहूय पुरा महर्षिरिदमुक्तवान् ।\nइषीकया मया बाल्यादेका विद्धा शकुन्तिका ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great sage once summoned Dharma and said: \"In childhood I pierced a small bird with a blade of grass."}},{"n":79,"text":"तत्किल्बिषं स्मरे धर्म नान्यत्पापमहं स्मरे ।\nतन्मे सहस्रसमितं कस्मान्नेहाजयत्तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I remember that fault, Dharma, and no other sin; why did my austerity, equal to a thousand times that, not erase it?"}},{"n":80,"text":"गरीयान्ब्राह्मणवधः सर्वभूतवधाद्यतः ।\nतस्मात्त्वं किल्बिषादस्माच्छूद्रयोनौ जनिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because killing a brahmin is graver than killing any other being, you will be born from a shudra womb for that fault.\""}},{"n":81,"text":"तेन शापेन धर्मोऽपि शूद्रयोनावजायत ।\nविद्वान्विदुररूपेण धार्मी तनुरकिल्बिषी ॥","meaning":{"en":"By that curse Dharma too was born from a shudra womb, as the learned Vidura, righteous, sinless of body."}},{"n":82,"text":"संजयो मुनिकल्पस्तु जज्ञे सूतो गवल्गणात् ।\nसूर्याच्च कुन्तिकन्यायां जज्ञे कर्णो महारथः ।\nसहजं कवचं बिभ्रत्कुण्डलोद्द्योतिताननः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, like a sage, was born as a Suta, from Gavalgana. Karna, the great chariot-warrior, was born from the Sun to Kunti the maiden, wearing a natural armor and with a face lit by earrings."}},{"n":83,"text":"अनुग्रहार्थं लोकानां विष्णुर्लोकनमस्कृतः ।\nवसुदेवात्तु देवक्यां प्रादुर्भूतो महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the favor of the worlds, Vishnu, to whom the worlds bow, of great fame, appeared as the son of Vasudeva by Devaki."}},{"n":84,"text":"अनादिनिधनो देवः स कर्ता जगतः प्रभुः ।\nअव्यक्तमक्षरं ब्रह्म प्रधानं निर्गुणात्मकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That god, without beginning or end, the maker and lord of the world, the unmanifest, the imperishable Brahman, the primal matter, beyond qualities,"}},{"n":85,"text":"आत्मानमव्ययं चैव प्रकृतिं प्रभवं परम् ।\nपुरुषं विश्वकर्माणं सत्त्वयोगं ध्रुवाक्षरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the unchanging Self, nature, the supreme source, the Person, the maker of all, in the state of sattva, the lasting imperishable one,"}},{"n":86,"text":"अनन्तमचलं देवं हंसं नारायणं प्रभुम् ।\nधातारमजरं नित्यं तमाहुः परमव्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the endless, unmoving god, the swan, Narayana the lord, the supporter, ageless, eternal, whom they call the supreme and unchanging:"}},{"n":87,"text":"पुरुषः स विभुः कर्ता सर्वभूतपितामहः ।\nधर्मसंवर्धनार्थाय प्रजज्ञेऽन्धकवृष्णिषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"that Person, all-pervading, maker, grandfather of all beings, was born among the Andhakas and Vrishnis to increase dharma."}},{"n":88,"text":"अस्त्रज्ञौ तु महावीर्यौ सर्वशस्त्रविशारदौ ।\nसात्यकिः कृतवर्मा च नारायणमनुव्रतौ ।\nसत्यकाद्धृदिकाच्चैव जज्ञातेऽस्त्रविशारदौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki and Kritavarman, two great heroes who knew missiles and were skilled in all weapons, were devoted to Narayana; they were born of Satyaka and of Hridika respectively."}},{"n":89,"text":"भरद्वाजस्य च स्कन्नं द्रोण्यां शुक्रमवर्धत ।\nमहर्षेरुग्रतपसस्तस्माद्द्रोणो व्यजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The seed of Bharadvaja, which fell in a vessel, grew; from that great sage of severe austerity Drona was born."}},{"n":90,"text":"गौतमान्मिथुनं जज्ञे शरस्तम्बाच्छरद्वतः ।\nअश्वत्थाम्नश्च जननी कृपश्चैव महाबलः ।\nअश्वत्थामा ततो जज्ञे द्रोणादस्त्रभृतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A pair of twins was born of Gautama, from Sharadvat, born in a clump of reeds: Ashvatthaman's mother, and the mighty Kripa. Then Ashvatthaman was born of Drona, best of weapon-bearers."}},{"n":91,"text":"तथैव धृष्टद्युम्नोऽपि साक्षादग्निसमद्युतिः ।\nवैताने कर्मणि तते पावकात्समजायत ।\nवीरो द्रोणविनाशाय धनुषा सह वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise Dhrishtadyumna, bright as the fire itself, was born from the fire at a great sacrifice, a mighty hero born with a bow to destroy Drona."}},{"n":92,"text":"तथैव वेद्यां कृष्णापि जज्ञे तेजस्विनी शुभा ।\nविभ्राजमाना वपुषा बिभ्रती रूपमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise Krishna, Draupadi, radiant and fair, was born from the altar, shining in body and bearing the finest beauty."}},{"n":93,"text":"प्रह्रादशिष्यो नग्नजित्सुबलश्चाभवत्ततः ।\nतस्य प्रजा धर्महन्त्री जज्ञे देवप्रकोपनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Subala and Nagnajit, a disciple of Prahlada, appeared; his offspring was one that destroys dharma, born from the gods' wrath."}},{"n":94,"text":"गान्धारराजपुत्रोऽभूच्छकुनिः सौबलस्तथा ।\nदुर्योधनस्य माता च जज्ञातेऽर्थविदावुभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni, son of Subala, was the son of the king of Gandhara, and Duryodhana's mother was born as well; both skilled in policy."}},{"n":95,"text":"कृष्णद्वैपायनाज्जज्ञे धृतराष्ट्रो जनेश्वरः ।\nक्षेत्रे विचित्रवीर्यस्य पाण्डुश्चैव महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From Krishna Dvaipayana was born Dhritarashtra, lord of men, and the mighty Pandu, on the wife of Vichitravirya."}},{"n":96,"text":"पाण्डोस्तु जज्ञिरे पञ्च पुत्रा देवसमाः पृथक् ।\nद्वयोः स्त्रियोर्गुणज्येष्ठस्तेषामासीद्युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Five sons were born to Pandu, equal to gods, each separately, by two wives; of them, Yudhishthira was the eldest in merit."}},{"n":97,"text":"धर्माद्युधिष्ठिरो जज्ञे मारुतात्तु वृकोदरः ।\nइन्द्राद्धनंजयः श्रीमान्सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira was born of Dharma, Vrikodara of Vayu, and the glorious Dhananjaya of Indra, best of all who bear weapons."}},{"n":98,"text":"जज्ञाते रूपसंपन्नावश्विभ्यां तु यमावुभौ ।\nनकुलः सहदेवश्च गुरुशुश्रूषणे रतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The twins, endowed with beauty, were born of the two Ashvins: Nakula and Sahadeva, devoted to serving their elders."}},{"n":99,"text":"तथा पुत्रशतं जज्ञे धृतराष्ट्रस्य धीमतः ।\nदुर्योधनप्रभृतयो युयुत्सुः करणस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise the wise Dhritarashtra had a hundred sons, led by Duryodhana, as well as Yuyutsu and Karana."}},{"n":100,"text":"अभिमन्युः सुभद्रायामर्जुनादभ्यजायत ।\nस्वस्रीयो वासुदेवस्य पौत्रः पाण्डोर्महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Abhimanyu was born to Arjuna by Subhadra, the sister's son of Vasudeva and the grandson of the great-souled Pandu."}},{"n":101,"text":"पाण्डवेभ्योऽपि पञ्चभ्यः कृष्णायां पञ्च जज्ञिरे ।\nकुमारा रूपसंपन्नाः सर्वशस्त्रविशारदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And to the five Pandavas, five sons were born by Draupadi, handsome princes skilled in all weapons."}},{"n":102,"text":"प्रतिविन्ध्यो युधिष्ठिरात्सुतसोमो वृकोदरात् ।\nअर्जुनाच्छ्रुतकीर्तिस्तु शतानीकस्तु नाकुलिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prativindhya was born from Yudhishthira, Sutasoma from Vrikodara, Shrutakirti from Arjuna, and Shatanika, son of Nakula."}},{"n":103,"text":"तथैव सहदेवाच्च श्रुतसेनः प्रतापवान् ।\nहिडिम्बायां च भीमेन वने जज्ञे घटोत्कचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise from Sahadeva came the mighty Shrutasena. And by Bhima, in the forest, Hidimba bore Ghatotkacha."}},{"n":104,"text":"शिखण्डी द्रुपदाज्जज्ञे कन्या पुत्रत्वमागता ।\nयां यक्षः पुरुषं चक्रे स्थूणः प्रियचिकीर्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhandi was born from Drupada, a girl who became a son, whom the yaksha Sthuna made a man out of a wish to please her."}},{"n":105,"text":"कुरूणां विग्रहे तस्मिन्समागच्छन्बहून्यथ ।\nराज्ञां शतसहस्राणि योत्स्यमानानि संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that war of the Kurus, many hundreds of thousands of kings came together, ready to fight in battle."}},{"n":106,"text":"तेषामपरिमेयानि नामधेयानि सर्वशः ।\nन शक्यं परिसंख्यातुं वर्षाणामयुतैरपि ।\nएते तु कीर्तिता मुख्या यैराख्यानमिदं ततम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their names are countless in every way, and could not be counted even in tens of thousands of years. But I have named the chief ones, through whom this account is spread."}}]}]}